WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.890
Thanks for waiting!

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:13.240
Today's guest is releasing their first album,
entitled <i>Melancholy Canary</i>, on July 24th.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.280
It's In NO Hurry to Shout!

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.660
Alice-san, you're the only member 
who can speak, correct?

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.370
Yes.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.510
There are a lot of questions 
I'd like to ask you.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.420
Let's see... For starters, 
what's your favorite food?

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.840
Chicken and onion skewers.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.220
Of all things, why chicken and onion skewers?!

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:39.240
I also like chicken rump meat.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.140
Come on!

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.760
What's the matter, Alice?

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.040
We're getting a ton of reactions on Twitter.

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.110
They think it's hilarious that you 
love chicken and onion skewers.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.240
I just thought about how much I liked it.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.330
Yuzu, you're spilling your milk! It's spilling!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.830
If you get any on the seat, you're dead!

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.210
Welcome to In NO Hurry.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.320
<i>It seems like I really</i>

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>love In NO Hurry a lot.</i>

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.000
Our Mikipedia page has been updated, too.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.740
"Vocalist: Alice."

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.090
"Due to her appearance, 
she is known as the Jet Black Fruit."

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.650
"Favorite food is chicken and onion skewers."

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.260
Vocalist, huh?

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.100
Haruyoshi-senpai?

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.150
Hey.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.820
Can we make Nino a guitarist and vocalist?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.150
What?!

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.160
Yana! Keep your hands on the wheel!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.650
Hang on. What do you mean?

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:45.040
I heard her sing while playing the guitar.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.290
It was her best performance yet.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.780
We can't pass on using that.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.280
Guitar? You mean...

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.230
Yeah.

00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:55.300
What do you think, Nino?

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:58.100
Don't you want to try 
playing it at Rock Horizon?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.170
<i>Playing Momo's guitar while</i>

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.680
<i>singing with In NO Hurry...</i>

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:07.820
Of course, the lead guitar will still be Yuzu.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.530
Nino, you'd be rhythm guitar.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.130
Visually, it's got impact, and it 
heats the music up even more.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.030
It sounds too good to pass up to me.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.780
It does sound good.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.910
Yana-san, I want to give it a try.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.780
All right.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.760
Let me hear it right now.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.600
<i>Whether I'm awake or asleep, I sing</i>

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.440
<i>I'm nothing more than a canary</i>

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.380
Stop.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.380
Rejected.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.510
True, it's not bad,
but it's missing something.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.790
It's not good enough for the stage yet,

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.480
and I can't let you perform that 
way at our first live concert.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:50.940
That's enough for now. Go home.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:56.150
Well, he's got a point. It's not there yet.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.770
But she only just started playing, 
and she's already this good.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.240
You're right.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.450
More importantly, putting everything together...

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.450
...felt really good!

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.990
Now I'm really fired up.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.740
How about we give it a go? It's been awhile.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:12.540
Give what a go?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.000
Training camp.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:49.510
♭10 The One Who Lit a Fire Inside Alice Was Me

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.930
Writing songs for Nino-chan?

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.760
Of course not.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.480
Nino's in the past now.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.980
In any case, now's not the 
time to write songs for her.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.470
I have to make more money

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.200
and quickly pay off what I owe.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.040
Did you look through this?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.910
Once I hand this in, I can go 
through with transferring schools.

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.910
I've signed it.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:16.390
Thanks.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.340
In the past, huh?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.480
Momo 
In NO Hurry is 
in no place to perform.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.480
What's with that punning four-eyes?

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.910
I heard you're going to have a training camp.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.720
Yeah.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.510
Every weekend at the studio 
until summer vacation.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.990
I remember doing that, too.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.140
Miou, I won't go after Yuzu at night. 
Rest easy. It's all good.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.830
How can you say that with a straight face?

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.680
And what's all good?

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.650
It's okay.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.750
In NO Hurry is a treasure that 
you and everyone else created.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.970
I'll take care of it.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.010
What's that supposed to mean?

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.740
Oh, you must be hungry.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.480
Sorry for talking so much.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.530
That's not it.

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:17.660
You can have this, too.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.400
Listen to me!

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:23.120
Well, Sakaki-kun,

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.610
good luck at your new school.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.920
Right. Thanks for everything.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.360
Transferring?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:36.680
Yeah.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.680
I see.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:40.160
<i>He's going away?</i>

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.260
<i>From here, too?</i>

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.540
<i>No! Why?</i>

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:49.050
I hate to admit it, but she 
pushed me to keep going.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.930
<i>I want to ask him, but I can't 
bring myself to turn around.</i>

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:54.970
Nino.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.350
Do you really intend to keep 
singing in that crappy band?

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:05.370
If you keep singing in a 
low-level band like that, you'll—

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.820
Take that back, Momo!

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.820
Don't insult In NO Hurry.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:14.290
To everyone there, and to me, 
it's a very precious place.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.360
All the songs are precious to us.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.160
Don't insult it.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.830
Precious?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.800
What's so good about his songs?

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.710
I...

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:27.050
can't breathe if I can't 
sing In NO Hurry's songs!

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.430
<i>Because I feel like I'll explode 
from my feelings for you.</i>

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.710
Big words.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.890
Even if you play at the festival, I doubt 
you'll be able to put on much of a show.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.020
How will we know if we don't try?

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.020
<i>Stop it.</i>

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.590
Then how about we see who's better?

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.480
<i>Just stop it, Momo.</i>

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.110
If my band wins...

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.020
<i>I just...</i>

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.280
...you quit In NO Hurry.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.990
No. I'll never participate 
in that kind of competition.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>I just want you to hear me, Momo.</i>

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:00.370
Right now, I don't want to sing 
for anyone but In NO Hurry.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.370
<i>I'm singing because 
I want to reach you, Momo.</i>

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.600
In any case, don't ever 
insult In NO Hurry again.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.180
I'm going now.

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.220
<i>That's all.</i>

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:14.840
<i>That's all.</i>

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.570
<i>That's all...</i>

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.180
<i>there is to it.</i>

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.000
Momo?

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:28.830
Struggle as much as you want.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.610
Have your screwed-up concert.

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:32.890
Just go.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:33.880
Wherever you want.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:39.790
<i>I thought,</i>

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.040
<i>when I saw Momo again,</i>

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.810
<i>that would be the finish line.</i>

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:46.960
<i>And yet...</i>

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.420
<i>And yet...</i>

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.420
<i>The more I see him, 
the farther away he gets.</i>

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:58.300
<i>I know I need to hurry up and make her 
just something from my past, but...</i>

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.680
Light Music Club

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.680
Yuzu, Kuro.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.180
The time table's up.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.150
We're the last slot, the best one.

00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:07.640
Wow, yeah! And that's the 
5,000-capacity stage, right?

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:09.010
Wait a second.

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.140
The black cats...

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.590
They're right behind us at the 
8,000-capacity stage, at the same time!

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:14.700
Sounds good.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.640
That makes things exciting.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.450
Now then, time to start the training camp!

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:22.950
This is the boys' room.

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:25.210
And this is the girls' room.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.460
Hey!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.090
What's with this difference?!

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:31.340
It wasn't like this when we 
did the training camp before.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.010
It's just because this girls' room is 
a recently renovated room that

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.970
the president uses as her nap room.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:42.720
President

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:40.300
She really took a liking to Alice 
after hearing about her love

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.720
for chicken and onion skewers, 
and said she could use it.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:46.340
I'll start offering chicken and onion skewers 
at the household shrine tomorrow.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:46.140
Thank you, 
onions and 
chicken

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:48.810
You sound like you'd really do it. That's scary.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.810
But she was so kind to me!

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:52.510
Just go.

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:53.690
Wherever you want.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.810
I will go. Wherever I want. 
I'll do what I want.

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:01.200
Alice, who are you talking to?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.810
So? I take it your sudden 
request for a training camp

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:08.120
means you haven't given up on 
Alice doing guitar and vocals.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.130
Of course!

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:13.320
All right, let's get changed 
and meet in the studio.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:15.880
Jeez.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.220
These kids are such a handful.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:23.290
The time table was your handiwork, wasn't it?

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:28.140
It had been decided that we'd be 
on the same stage as In NO Hurry.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.060
I told them that given the 
value of Kiryuu Momo's name,

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.430
we could pull off the 8,000-capacity stage.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.280
And it'd be interesting to have the two 
masked bands play at the same time.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.750
Are you just playing with us?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.900
So? What's your next play? 
What is it you want to do?

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:47.000
I wonder why your puns 
always make me so angry.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:50.000
I just like interesting things.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.340
It came to me when I picked you up, too.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.420
That I'd definitely get something 
interesting out of this.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.770
That's my only instinct that's never wrong.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.720
Thanks for the hard work.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.310
You'd better fill that capacity of 8,000.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:13.560
Forget 8,000. I'll meet 
the whole venue's capacity.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.470
Honestly...

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.800
He's so desperate to push forward.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:29.670
<i>Even if I'm completely naked, 
I'm not scared anymore</i>

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.640
<i>I'll keep on singing, because I'm a canary</i>

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:40.100
Not quite there yet, Ninocchi.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.160
You dragged a bit in some places.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.730
All you can do is keep practicing.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.850
One more try from the top.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.340
All right, let's go.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.350
Yeah!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.040
<i>Momo.</i>

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:59.610
<i>I'll struggle and struggle 
and struggle all I can.</i>

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.810
<i>Fly!</i>

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.830
<i>After all,</i>

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:09.310
<i>I have this guitar!</i>

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.750
All right!

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:15.460
That's the end of our first 
day of training camp.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.710
O-One more try... from the...

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.420
You're staggering like an old lady!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.410
Oh, right, Alice.

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.510
I'm writing a new song.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.760
I wanted to add it to our set. 
Will you be okay?

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.000
Of course, I'll be fine.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.980
I'll show Momo.

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:34.450
That we won't lose to the black cats.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:36.810
Alice, did something...

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:37.690
What?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:42.490
No, uh... I'm having trouble with the lyrics, 
so it'll be a while until it's finished.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:43.850
Roger.

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.520
Anyway, I'm hungry.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.620
True.

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.660
I want to eat something light.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.800
Then how about we have a soumen party?

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.850
Who bought all this ham?

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.960
It's raw ham, roasted ham, and thigh ham.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.170
The triple crown of ham.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.630
Who are you, Professor Ham?!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.350
Everyone loves ham.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.590
Why do you sound so stiff?!

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.350
Let's get this done quickly.

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.010
I'm starving.

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:13.600
Wow! You're so good. Just like a mother!

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.310
I cut the cucumbers.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.800
What kind of cutting style is that?!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.900
And so many! Did you invite 
a kappa or something?!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.830
Everyone loves cucumbers.

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.230
Again, why so stiff?!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:24.810
Ninocchi and Haruyoshi-senpai have changed.

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:25.680
Yeah.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.730
Time to eat.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.830
How is it, Ninocchi? Delicious, right?

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.630
Alice, aren't you eating too much?

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:48.070
That's way too much! Is it that good?

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.470
I guess your cook was just that good.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.370
Even if the noodles are swept away, 
this feeling won't be swept away!

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.810
<i>I want to know more about them.</i>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.620
<i>I want to keep going with all of them.</i>

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.230
Yuzu.

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.200
Have you showered already?

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.220
Oh, yeah. You, too?

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:06.870
Yep.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:09.720
When's your birthday?

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.100
May 5th.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.560
Blood type?

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:13.520
A.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.080
You're drinking milk again.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.920
"Yuzu likes drinking milk."

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.840
What's with you? Why are you taking notes?

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.960
I thought I'd try to learn 
more about everyone.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.220
Yeah?

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:28.270
Oh, Yuzu, do you have someone you like?

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.420
What are you asking all of a sudden?!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:32.350
Serious

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.310
Do you?

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:32.350
I want to know.

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:34.830
I...

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:36.890
I do.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.690
Why do you look so gloomy all of a sudden?!

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.780
I'm sorry. You have someone you like, 
and I made you kiss me back then.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.500
I-I already said that was all my fault!

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:52.750
A-And besides, that wasn't my first time.

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:54.240
What? Really?

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:55.890
It was my first time.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:56.750
It was?

00:14:56.970 --> 00:14:59.920
Amazing, Yuzu. You're an adult, 
even though you're so small.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:03.380
That's a few words too many! 
And take off that mask!

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.660
When did you first start liking that person?

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.850
Q-Quite a long time ago.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.290
So you're just like me.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.900
And what do you like about that person?

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:15.740
That's a secret.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.750
What do you like about Momo?

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.900
Maybe... the voice he calls my name with?

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:28.530
He was always with me, 
for as long as I can remember.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.130
I'm not sure I even know 
what I like about him.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.530
But six years ago, when he disappeared,

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:37.490
I felt like I lost a part of myself.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.890
That's... weird, isn't it?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.420
Yeah. I get it.

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:48.230
Yuzu, you know what?

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:50.650
I was worried about the concert.

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.180
But, somehow...

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:57.120
I've started to look forward to it.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.410
Oh? Is that right?

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.150
Nino.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:30.820
Huh?

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:34.470
I was talking to Yuzu and...

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:37.970
Come on, Alice! Just a 
little more! You can do it!

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:42.350
That's right. I was talking about what 
I like about Momo, and in the middle, I—

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:43.720
...that crappy band.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.980
Have your screwed-up concert.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.500
Why does he have to make 
fun of In NO Hurry so much?!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.200
Ow, that hurt.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.910
<i>I don't have time for this.</i>

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.570
<i>Anyway, time to research!</i>

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:00.140
<i>What is this summer festival?</i>

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.330
<i>The top summer music 
festival for Japanese music,</i>

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:05.160
<i>Rock Horizon.</i>

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.420
<i>Lots of artists</i>

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.550
<i>play music here.</i>

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.440
<i>And...</i>

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.460
<i>This is the stage we'll perform on.</i>

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.060
<i>I am Alice.</i>

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.060
<i>I won't let anyone call us "screwed-up."</i>

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:28.310
<i>I won't let anyone insult our In NO Hurry.</i>

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:31.800
<i>I have to make sure we don't fail.</i>

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.860
I see.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:35.330
<i>When he said that...</i>

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.660
<i>When he called it "screwed-up,"</i>

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.620
<i>he meant me.</i>

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.330
<i>Everyone else is perfect.</i>

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:44.620
<i>Because if I</i>

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.330
<i>go berserk again,</i>

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.810
<i>I might actually screw it all up for real.</i>

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:52.410
<i>Momo could see that.</i>

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:04.450
<i>Even if I'm completely naked, 
I'm not scared anymore</i>

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.310
<i>I'll keep on singing, because I'm a canary</i>

00:18:13.890 --> 00:18:16.210
What happened, Nino?

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:18.610
You've learned how to 
play perfectly overnight.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.620
I have to do better.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:25.910
Pluck Pluck Pluck Pluck

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:25.910
Better, better, better, better, better.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.630
What's with her? It's kind of scary.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:25.500
You've got a point. She's going like a demon.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.810
But what is it?

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.000
It's like it isn't really working.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.170
In fact, I feel like the way she was 
before was more interesting.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>When I sing, that alone makes me wonderful</i>

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>I have to sing well.</i>

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:47.970
<i>So let me stay in this cage</i>

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:54.400
<i>When I shout, that alone makes me invincible</i>

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:53.890
<i>Perfect, with no mistakes.</i>

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:58.440
<i>So please don't open this cage</i>

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:57.690
<i>I have to make sure that stage is packed.</i>

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:03.200
<i>I'll fall</i>

00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:02.620
<i>I have to do better with 
both the guitar and vocals.</i>

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>Better!</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:09.380
<i>Straight down</i>

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:06.620
<i>Better!</i>

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.550
Alice, you're acting strange.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.310
Huh?

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:18.880
Why do you keep thinking you 
have to do better and better?

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:22.220
Because I want to make 
our concert a success.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.310
Is that all?

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:27.500
Well, if I go berserk again, 
I'll make trouble for everyone.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.090
So I have to get better to make up for that.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:32.980
Stupid.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.890
That kind of performance is boring.

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.820
Stuff it full of emotion, like usual.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:43.140
Ambition and a solid skill base are important, 
but more than that is how it feels.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:47.100
Whether you like it our not, the feelings you 
put into your music always come through.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.330
Don't attack with technique. 
Attack with emotion.

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:52.580
Even if you do go berserk, we'll be there.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.850
What's wrong with screwing up?

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:56.370
That makes it more fun.

00:19:56.370 --> 00:19:59.050
Throw more of how you feel into 
it than you ever have, Alice.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:02.020
Even more so if you want to reach Momo.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:07.430
Want to try singing whatever 
lyrics you come up with just once?

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.810
Sing with your own words.

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:12.310
Good idea.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:13.310
Yeah.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:15.370
<i>Attack with emotion.</i>

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.660
<i>I never thought about doing that before.</i>

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.110
<i>Yuzu, don't blame me</i>

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:23.920
<i>for whatever happens.</i>

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.390
<i>Momo's stupid!</i>

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:45.720
<i>Whether he's asleep or awake, 
he doesn't understand anything</i>

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:48.090
<i>He's way too picky</i>

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:52.600
<i>So he's just a boring idiot! Stupid!</i>

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.110
<i>His hair is too long, and he's annoying</i>

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.360
<i>I can't hear him when he mumbles</i>

00:20:58.790 --> 00:20:59.750
<i>Momo.</i>

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:03.410
<i>Can't he speak a little more clearly?</i>

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:00.940
<i>Momo.</i>

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:02.640
<i>Momo.</i>

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:04.340
<i>Momo.</i>

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.220
<i>I don't care about Momo anymore!</i>

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:18.500
Alice.

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.000
How long are you going to practice?

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.210
Singing with your own words really

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.230
lets you see things for how they are.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:30.170
Momo doesn't feel anything for me anymore.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:31.970
And yet, I...

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:34.640
I still let his words control me.

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:37.020
What am I doing?

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.150
A-Are you crying?

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:40.790
I am not!

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.570
You totally look like you will!

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:43.920
I won't cry.

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:45.360
I'll never cry.

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:47.720
Not over him.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.830
Damn him.

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:56.120
If you want to cry, just do it.

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:57.880
I'll pretend not to see it.

00:21:59.230 --> 00:22:00.810
I won't cry.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:03.170
Alice, you sure are stubborn!

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:05.530
But...

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:09.180
Lyrics are amazing, aren't they?

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.450
Once I made the lyrics into my own words,

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:17.480
I felt like I truly sang for the first time.

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:21.730
<i>The one who always lights 
a fire inside Alice is Momo.</i>

00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.240
Can I ask a favor?

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:29.740
You said you were writing a new song, right?

00:22:30.300 --> 00:22:33.230
<i>But that day alone was different.</i>

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:34.240
The lyrics...

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.290
Can I try writing them?

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:43.490
<i>The one who lit a fire inside Alice</i>

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:45.240
<i>was me.</i>

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:52.150
♭11 
I'll Make It So All of Them Can Never Leave
